{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["<b>An ox or a sheep or a goat</b> is juxtaposed to a gentile's son, to teach that a obligatory offering is accepted only from an Israelite." "<b>And when seven days etc.</b> The Holy One, blessed be He, said: if he slaughters on the first day, it appears as if he slaughters for the sake of heaven and earth, which were created on day one. And if on day two, it appears as if he slaughters for the sake of the firmament, which was made on day two. And on day three, for the sake of the sea and dry land. And on day four, for the sake of the luminaries. And on day five, for the sake of the creeping things. And on day six, for the sake of man. Rather, he should wait seven days and know that I created the world in six days and rested on the seventh, and he slaughters for My name's sake."], :book :leviticus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:20:18.710566393Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}